@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About · Caustikon</PageTitle>

<h1>About</h1>
<p class="lede">Caustikon is two .NET packages and this site. The packages are the product; the site runs them in your browser so the numbers can be inspected without installing anything.</p>

<h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
<p>
    Every catalogued glass is transcribed from the RefractiveIndex.INFO database, which Mikhail Polyanskiy released into the public
    domain under CC0 1.0. The database in turn transcribes manufacturer catalogs; each entry here names that catalog release,
    links to the entry's file in the database, and records the date the database was read. The current import is commit
    @manifestCommit, read on @retrieved.
</p>
<p>
    Of @totalEntries manufacturer entries in the database, @SiteInfo.GlassCount have closed-form dispersion and are included.
    The rest are tabulated-only (filters, some infrared and matching materials) and are listed by path and reason in the
    repository's <a href="https://github.com/levvs-one/caustikon/blob/main/data/glasses/manifest.json" rel="noopener">manifest</a>.
</p>
<p>
    Colour uses the CIE 1931 2° observer at 1 nm and illuminant D65 at 5 nm, copied unchanged from the colour-science project's
    data tables (BSD-3-Clause). Licences and citations: <a href="https://github.com/levvs-one/caustikon/blob/main/DATA-LICENSE.md" rel="noopener">DATA-LICENSE.md</a>.
</p>

<h2>How the numbers are checked</h2>
<p>
    A dispersion fit and the printed n<sub>d</sub> of a glass are two independent statements by the manufacturer. On every commit,
    the test suite evaluates all @SiteInfo.GlassCount models at the exact d, F and C lines and compares with the printed n<sub>d</sub>
    and ν<sub>d</sub>. The bound on n<sub>d</sub> is five units in the fifth decimal plus the rounding of the printed value; the bound
    on ν<sub>d</sub> is that bound propagated through its definition. All pass. The largest deviation in the catalog, and which glass
    it belongs to, is recorded in the manifest.
</p>
<p>
    N-BK7 is pinned further, to the SCHOTT datasheet of 1 December 2023: seven internal-transmittance rows at 10 mm and 25 mm
    and nine dn/dT cells across three temperature ranges and three lines, each within the datasheet's printed precision.
    D65 through a perfect transmitter reproduces the D65 white point.
</p>

<h2>What is not modelled</h2>
<p>
    Absorption is bulk only, from tabulated k; there is no scattering, no coating, no surface roughness. The index of air is 1 and
    does not change with temperature or pressure, so temperature results are absolute-index shifts. There is no birefringence,
    no polarization state beyond s and p power fractions at an interface, no thin-film interference, no diffraction. The
    packages compute what happens at a plane dielectric boundary and in a homogeneous slab; scene geometry, lenses and rendering
    belong to the caller.
</p>

<h2>Packages</h2>
<pre><code>dotnet add package Caustikon
dotnet add package Caustikon.Glasses</code></pre>
<p>
    <code>Caustikon</code> is the mathematics: refraction, Fresnel, the dispersion models. <code>Caustikon.Glasses</code> is the
    catalog with absorption, temperature and colour. Both target .NET 8 and .NET 10 with no dependencies beyond the base class
    library. Source, issues and the data of record are on
    <a href="https://github.com/levvs-one/caustikon" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>, under the MIT licence.
</p>

<h2>Citing</h2>
<p>
    For the glass data cite M. N. Polyanskiy, "Refractiveindex.info database of optical constants", <em>Scientific Data</em> 11, 94 (2024),
    and the manufacturer catalog named in the glass's provenance. For the code cite the repository and the version shown in the footer.
</p>

@code {
    private string manifestCommit = "c5c2f18";
    private string retrieved = "2026-09-05";
    private int totalEntries = 1784;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        GlassProvenance provenance = GlassCatalog.All[0].Provenance;
        int at = provenance.Source.IndexOf("commit ", StringComparison.Ordinal);
        if (at >= 0)
        {
            manifestCommit = provenance.Source[(at + 7)..].Split(',')[0];
        }

        retrieved = provenance.RetrievedOn.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    }
}
